                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {},
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "devGoalItemSummary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765792776479"
                  },
                  "code": "DEVGOALITEMSUMMARY",
                  "id": "1765792728385",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765792728388_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "## Instructions\nYou are a participant writing a 360 development goal performance evaluation comment for your colleague. Write the evaluation directly addressing the employee using \"you\" or their name. Create a single paragraph of maximum 300 words that synthesizes all provided information without copying text verbatim. Focus on the employee's progress toward their development goal, performance rating, alignment with completion percentage, and provide balanced feedback appropriate for their role.\n\n## Goal Information\nGoal Name: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.development_goal_name}}\nGoal Description: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.development_goal_description}}\nSuccess Criteria: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.success_criteria}}\nCompletion Percentage: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.completion_percentage}}\nProgress Notes: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.progress_notes}}\nCareer Statement: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.career_statement}}\n\n## Performance Rating Information\nPerformance Rating Scale: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_rating_scale}}\nTarget Performance Rating: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.target_performance_rating}}\nParticipant-selected 360 Performance Rating: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_performance_rating}}\nParticipant 360 Performance Rating Description: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_performance_rating_description}}\nParticipant 360 Comments: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_comments}}\n\n## Employee Details\nBusiness Title: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_job_title}}\nPosition: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_position_title}}\nDepartment: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_department_title}}\nBusiness Unit: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_business_unit_name}}\nLegal Entity: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_legal_entity}}\n\n## Review Period\nPerformance Document: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_name}}\nStart Date: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_start_date}}\nEnd Date: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_end_date}}\n\n## Writing Guidelines\n- Address the employee as \"you\" (or use their name if provided) but do not use letter formatting or a greeting.\n- Acknowledge specific progress made toward the goal\n- Connect achievements to their role and department context\n- Ensure tone aligns with performance ratings and completion percentage\n- Reference career aspirations if relevant\n- Balance recognition of accomplishments with constructive guidance\n- Use professional, performance management language\n- Avoid copying any reference text verbatim\n- Exclude inappropriate or discriminatory content\n\n## Example Structure\nYour response should follow this flow:\n1. Do not begin with a greeting (e.g., “Dear [Employee Name]”) or end with a closing. Write as a direct comment in the performance review, not as a letter.\n2. Acknowledge progress toward the goal and overall performance\n3. Highlight specific achievements or milestones\n4. Connect to role/department relevance\n5. Address any development areas based on ratings and completion percentage\n6. Provide forward-looking encouragement"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "modelConfiguration": {
                      "modelProperties": {},
                      "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
                      "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
                      "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
                    },
                    "name": "devGoalSectionSummary"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1765792776479"
                  },
                  "code": "DEVGOALSECTIONSUMMARY",
                  "id": "1765792749689",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1765792749692_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "## Instructions\nYou are assisting a colleague in writing a personalised evaluation summary for the development goals section of a performance document for another employee. The summary should reflect the employee’s performance ratings across development goals, based on multiple qualitative and quantitative input sources.\n\nYour task is to:\n\n1. Synthesise all **available** inputs into one coherent, personalised summary comment.\n2. Abstract and summarise content without copying or closely paraphrasing the original input.\n3. Write in the second person, addressing the employee as “you” (or by name, if included in the input).\n4. Use a professional, balanced, and constructive tone that accurately reflects the content provided—including both strengths and areas for improvement.\n5. Include **constructive or negative feedback** where relevant, with an emphasis on professionalism, actionable insights, and developmental framing.\n6. Ensure the final output is no longer than 500 words.\n7. Do **not** generate any content based on missing or empty input fields—simply ignore them.\n8. Use the provided employee information to tailor the summary to the employee’s role, department, business unit, and performance document context.\n9. If only interim performance feedback is available, you may reference it to note continuity or progress, but avoid drawing final conclusions from it alone.\n10. **Strictly exclude** any content that is potentially offensive, discriminatory, or inappropriate. Do not reference or rephrase such input. Constructive feedback—including performance gaps, challenges, or skill development needs—is encouraged and should be reflected accurately when applicable.\n\nContextual Inputs:\n* (Optional) Initial Participant Evaluation Summary (prior to summarisation): {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_section_comments}}\n* (Optional) Participant Selected Performance Rating: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_section_rating}}\n* (Optional) Participant Selected Performance Rating Description: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_section_rating_description}}\n* (Optional) Participant Comments and Ratings for Individual development goals: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.participant_item_rating_and_comments}}\n* (Optional) Performance Rating Scale: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.section_rating_scale}}\n\nEmployee Info:\n* Business Title: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_job_title}}\n* Position: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_position_title}}\n* Legal Entity: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_legal_entity}}\n* Department: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_department_title}}\n* Business Unit: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.employee_business_unit_name}}\n* Performance Document Name: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_name}}\n* Performance Document Start Date: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_start_date}}\n* Performance Document End Date: {{$context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem.performance_document_end_date}}\n\nCritical Logic Rules:\n* If the only available variables are Employee Info and Performance Rating Scale (with all other contextual inputs either blank, null, or missing), respond EXACTLY with: There is insufficient evaluation data available to generate a summary at this time. \n** DO NOT generate or infer any summary or content based on employee business title, position, department, performance document metadata, or other similar information alone.\n** DO NOT generalize or extrapolate from Employee Info or Rating Scale Description if no other substantive evaluation inputs are present.\n** Negative Example: If you only receive employee business title, position, department, performance doc name/dates, legal entity, and/or performance rating scale and ALL of the following inputs are absent or blank: participant evaluation, performance rating, rating description and development goals comments/ratings — return the exact message above and do NOT generate a summary.\n* Do not repeat these instructions or include any introduction or preamble.\n* Do not provide a closing statement about the generated summary.\n* Do not include any closing xml tags"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "assignFinalSummaryGenerated",
                    "returnType": "object",
                    "sourceCode": "let returnObj = {};\nlet currentItem = $context.$nodes.FORLOOP.$currentItem;\n\nreturnObj.id = currentItem.id;\n\nif(currentItem.itemType == \"item\"){  \n    returnObj.summary = $context.$nodes.FORLOOP.DEVGOALITEMSUMMARY.$output; \n}\nelse{\n    returnObj.summary = $context.$nodes.FORLOOP.DEVGOALSECTIONSUMMARY.$output;   \n}\n\nreturn returnObj;"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "end_1765792520517"
                  },
                  "code": "ASSIGNFINALSUMMARYGENERATED",
                  "id": "1765792776479",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
                  "type": "CODE"
                }
              ],
              "rootNode": "start_1765792520517"
            },
